      "text": "To solve for the two positive real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) given their geometric and harmonic means, we can utilize the following relationships:\n\n1. Geometric Mean:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we obtain:\n\\[\nab = 3\n\\]\n\n2. Harmonic Mean:\n\\[\n\\frac{2ab}{a + b} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nWe can now solve these equations simultaneously. First, we can express \\(a + b\\) in terms of \\(ab\\):\n\\[\na + b = \\frac{2ab}{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{2ab \\cdot 2}{3} = \\frac{4ab}{3}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(ab = 3\\) into this equation:\n\\[\na + b = \\frac{4 \\cdot 3}{3} = 4\n\\]\n\nSo we have:\n\\[\nab = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad a + b = 4\n\\]\n\nThese equations are the roots of a quadratic equation, \\(x^2 - (a+b)x + ab = 0\\). Substituting \\(a + b = 4\\) and \\(ab = 3\\), we get:\n\\[\nx^2 - 4x + 3 = 0\n\\]\n\nHowever, this quadratic equation factors nicely:\n\\[\n(x - 1)(x - 3) = 0\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[\nx = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = 3\n\\]\n\nHence, the two numbers are \\(1\\) and \\(3\\). Let's verify our results using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define symbols\r\na, b = symbols('a b')\r\n\r\n# Geometric mean\r\ngeo_mean_eq = Eq(a * b, 3)\r\n\r\n# Harmonic mean\r\nharmonic_mean_eq = Eq((2 * a * b) / (a + b), 3 / 2)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolutions = solve((geo_mean_eq, harmonic_mean_eq), (a, b))\r\n\r\nprint(solutions)\n```\n```output\n[(1.00000000000000, 3.00000000000000), (3.00000000000000, 1.00000000000000)]\n```\nThe solutions obtained from the system of equations are:\n\n\\[\n(a, b) = (1, 3) \\quad \\text{or} \\quad (3, 1)\n\\]\n\nThus, the two positive real numbers are \\(\\boxed{1, 3}\\).",
